  "body": "Seen by a worker's quick gate on 2026-11-12 (PR #1179's report) and on origin/main without that change.\n\n`cargo test -p xtask` fails one unit test: `no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app` reports the Gate map of `crates/app/tests/lathe_post_css.rs` naming `app::post`. PR #965 (merged today) added that check and corrected 134 suite headers to name the crate a module really lives in (`post::post`, not `app::post`); PR #990 (merged later, by hand, as part of #1058's stack) brought in `lathe_post_css.rs` with the old-style header. Two merges that crossed.\n\nWhy P1: the gate tool's own unit tests are red on main, so every quick gate that touches `xtask/` fails, and the header means a change in the post crate does not select this suite.\n\nDone means: the suite's `Gate map` header names the owning crates (`post::post` and whatever else it covers that moved out of `app`); `cargo test -p xtask` is green; a grep shows no other suite header added since #965 still names a moved module as `app::` (list any you fix).",
